{"name":"Blaze","hex":"#fa8c4f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blaze","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A male given name from Latin.","A surname originating as a patronymic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blaze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blaze (1989 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blaze is a 1989 American comedy-drama film written and directed by Ron Shelton, based on the 1974 memoir Blaze Starr: My Life as Told to Huey Perry by Blaze Starr and Huey Perry. The film stars Paul Newman as Earl Long and Lolita Davidovich as Blaze Starr."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Blaze_imp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blaze_(1989_film)","wikidata":"Q883197"},{"title":"Blaze (2018 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blaze is a 2018 American biographical drama film directed by Ethan Hawke based on the life of country musician Blaze Foley. The screenplay by Hawke and Sybil Rosen was adapted from the memoir Living in the Woods in a Tree: Remembering Blaze Foley by Rosen. It stars musician Ben Dickey as Foley. The film premiered at the 2018 Sundance Film Festival and was released in the United States on August 17, 2018, by IFC Films."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3c/Blaze_%282018_movie_poster%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blaze_(2018_film)","wikidata":"Q29011389"},{"title":"Blaze (group)","blocks":[{"text":"Blaze is an American house music group formed in New Jersey in 1984."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blaze_(group)","wikidata":"Q883182"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3c/Blaze_%282018_movie_poster%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3c/Blaze_%282018_movie_post